  "summary": "FieldSchema now declares the deadline semantic on date and datetime fields. dueLike is an optional boolean with no default. settledWhen is an optional EvaluatedExpressionInputSchema: a per-record CEL predicate in the visibleWhen family. Both are refused off DEADLINE_FIELD_TYPES (date, datetime), and settledWhen is refused unless dueLike: true; this is a superRefine over a type set, the maxLength/valueDomain/rows idiom. The lint field-rule pass (validate-expressions.ts) judges settledWhen exactly as it judges visibleWhen: it must parse, read record.FIELD and not a bare field, name a declared field, and read only FIELD_RULE_BOUND_ROOTS. That pass runs at os build, os validate and the object save door. The field form offers both keys, settledWhen only once the field is a deadline. The docs page fields.mdx teaches them. The showcase task, todo task and crm activity declare dueLike plus settledWhen, settled on their measured status values done, completed and completed. Mechanism hypotheses: H1 held, with no conversion. Zero spec-validated sources spell dueLike, ListColumnSchema refuses it with unrecognized_keys, and the widening needs no ADR-0087 disposition (check-adr-0087-registration judges breaking declarations only). H2 measured: the bound roots are record, previous and parent; today() is a stdlib function and applies; value is a bare reference and is refused; no new scope name was added. H3 held: superRefine over a set. H4 measured as above. Nine files outside the claim's declared surface were touched. Each is a classification ratchet that a new FieldSchema key or CEL slot turns red, and no open PR touches any of them (deviations). CI on head a520b4eea5 was in_progress at report time: 9 check runs completed, 23 in progress.",
  "mechanism_hypotheses": {
    "H1": "Held, with no conversion. git grep dueLike|settledWhen at dee7692f0b: 3 hits, all CHANGELOG.md prose (console, platform-objects, spec), no source. ListColumnSchema.safeParse({field:'due_date', dueLike:true}) gives unrecognized_keys [dueLike]; the control {field:'due_date'} parses. No ADR-0087 entry. The changeset is a widening, and check-adr-0087-registration exits 0 (breakingDeclaration: 'widening adds NO signal').",
    "H2": "Measured. The field-rule family's bound roots are FIELD_RULE_BOUND_ROOTS = record, previous, parent. today() is a stdlib function present in every CEL env, not a scope name, and passes. value is not in SCOPE_ROOTS, reads as a bare reference, and is refused. current_user gets the family's root verdict naming settledWhen. All are pinned in validate-expressions.test.ts. The server-side gates (the parent gate, the null guard, the traversal refusal) stay off settledWhen, as they are off visibleWhen.",
    "H3": "Held. field.zod.ts scopes a type-specific key with a superRefine over a ReadonlySet of types (BOUNDED_STRING / VALUE_DOMAIN / MULTILINE_EDITOR), not with a discriminated variant. DEADLINE_FIELD_TYPES follows that idiom: dueLike on text is a custom issue at [dueLike].",
    "H4": "Measured. showcase_task status has done, so the predicate is record.status == 'done'. todo_task has completed, which also matches the app's documented overdue definition. crm_activity has completed. crm_activity also has cancelled, and app-todo has deferred; see open_questions."
  },
